<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-3875] Groups are not derived when using ActiveDirectory</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3875</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;ActiveDirectoryGroupRealm is using &quot;userPrincipalName&quot; for deriving groups that user belongs to, however:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;this field is not mandatory in ActiveDirectory&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;can contain user email where domain is different from REALM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;in such a scenario user is able to log in but no groups are derived&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;this was also mentioned in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/986&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/986&lt;/a&gt; but never resolved&lt;/p&gt;</description>
